-- title:
--   Two branch primes over p on the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $p$ and $M$ with $p$ prime and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and hypotheses $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, together with the assumption that every unit of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$ already lies in $H$. Assume $\mathrm{jqModC}\ \mathbb{Q}$, the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the integral $j$-numerator series, lies in the $q$-expansion function field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \top$ of the full modular group, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, i.e. a bundle of data comprising the properness, flatness, integrality, normality and finite presentation of the two-chart integral model `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` over the base ring `R p`, the corresponding properness and relative-dimension-one smoothness at level `ΓN p M H hpM`, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` identified with the geometric generic fibre and pinned by $q$-expansions, Galois equivariance, generic smoothness and geometric integrality, and, for each place datum, two component morphisms `comp`. Then there is a pair $P_0, P_1$ of ideals of the $j$-finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj` (the $R p$-subalgebra of the $q$-expansion function field of `ΓM M H` attached to the chart parameter $j$), each a minimal prime of the ideal generated by $p$, with $P_0 \neq P_1$, such that the following holds for every valuation subring $A$ of the algebraic closure of $\mathbb{Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$, whose residue field has characteristic $p$ and is algebraically closed, every ring homomorphism $\rho : R p \to A$ whose composite with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is the structure map, every $i \in \{0,1\}$, every point $y$ of the fibre of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along the residue map of $\rho$, and every prime $\mathfrak{q}$ of the chart algebra: if the first pullback projection sends $y$ to the image of $\mathfrak{q}$ under the finite-chart immersion `ιFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, and if $y$ lies in the image of the base map of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ \rho\ i$, then $P_i \subseteq \mathfrak{q}$. In particular the same pair of primes works simultaneously for all places $A$ over $p$.
--
--   This locates, on the $j$-finite chart of the integral model, the two components of the Deligne–Rapoport fibre of $X_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ exactly dividing $M$: each component's image is contained in the vanishing locus of one of two distinct minimal primes over $p$, and the indexing is uniform in the chosen place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ above $p$. It is used downstream to separate the two components by a chart function, to compute preimages of the closures of their images, and to show that the two branch points on the two charts are distinct.
